WEBVTT

00:07:59.236 --> 00:08:00.236
A smaller scale,

00:08:00.236 --> 00:08:01.476
but it’s already doing it.

00:08:01.476 --> 00:08:04.316
This is Climeworks and Carbfix in Iceland.

00:08:04.676 --> 00:08:07.796
They're using geothermal heat to power it,

00:08:07.796 --> 00:08:11.076
and they’re putting the CO2
into the Icelandic basaltic rock.

00:08:13.276 --> 00:08:16.876
So one issue, though,
with direct air capture,

00:08:16.876 --> 00:08:19.116
is it takes a lot of energy
to power those fans.

00:08:20.116 --> 00:08:22.116
And that energy obviously has to be green.

00:08:22.156 --> 00:08:23.156
It has to be clean;

00:08:23.156 --> 00:08:24.796
you can’t use fossil fuels for it.

00:08:24.836 --> 00:08:28.676
But it also makes it much more expensive
than other techniques.

00:08:28.916 --> 00:08:31.596
And it takes energy to cook wood
and to grind rock,